/* English question bank — Le Benchmark des Makers. TRANSLATED, NOT REVIEWED YET.

   The French bank is the reference text and this file is its translation,
   question by question, in the same order, with THE SAME ANSWER ORDER: the
   correct answer stays at index 0 and the engine shuffles at render time. A
   translation that moves the right answer breaks scoring silently, and no test
   catches it, because the shape stays valid.

   The old English questions in `makers-benchmark/index.html` are NOT the
   source. They were generic, they were rewritten from scratch in French, and
   restoring them would undo that work. The artifact is a reference for layout
   and colour only. Not one of those questions was reused here.

   `p` is the difficulty step (1, 2, 3) inside the tier. The 9 questions of each
   tier are ordered 1-1-1 / 2-2-2 / 3-3-3, in that order, exactly as in
   `tracks.ts`. `tests/benchmark-bank.test.ts` enforces that shape on both
   languages.

   Translation decisions worth knowing about, since they are not obvious from
   the diff:

   - Currency stays in euros, as in the French. The figures are part of the
     scenario, not a localisation: an amount converted to dollars would change
     what the question is asking.
   - `<code>` fragments, tool names, file names and protocol names are left
     untouched: they are identifiers, not copy.
   - French typographic quotes are rendered as ordinary English quotes. The
     answer text is compared by the engine as a string, so nothing depends on
     them, but they read wrong in English.
   - Track names (Marketing & Growth, Engineering & Tech, Process & Ops,
     Finance & RevOps) were already English in the French file and are kept. */

